1 | devops | Fix the findings raised against PR 2765 on branch docs/settlement-empirical-check. Read the review comment on issue 2340 whose first line reads CRITIC SETTLEMENT EMPIRICAL CHECK before touching anything, and treat its file and line citations as the specification. DOCS ONLY, and stay inside docs/operations/deployment.md unless a finding names another file. F2 IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS AND YOU SHOULD FIX IT FIRST. The remedy as written can ship the money losing position. Take the wrong result branch where the environment reads off or absent while the running build posts card settlement: the doc tells the reader to run make deploy-web and separately tells them not to correct the Vercel value. An operator following both literally redeploys the BALANCE build into production, which is the exact state where Olympus pays for the ticket, which is the loss this whole section exists to prevent. The doc is right that an env edit alone leaves the running bundle untouched. What it omits is that a redeploy CONVERGES the running bundle onto whatever the environment holds at that moment, validated or not. Gate the redeploy: before deploying, confirm the environment value is the INTENDED position, and if it is absent or unintended, restore it FIRST and only then redeploy. Rewrite the do not correct the value line so it forbids only silently rewriting the environment to match an observation and calling it fixed, and does NOT forbid restoring a variable that was deleted. F1, also HIGH: the baseline vercel env ls command does not run in a clone that is not linked to the project, the error goes to stderr, so the pipe yields nothing and the reader sees empty output. The doc separately defines empty output as one of the two wrong result signatures, so a tooling failure manufactures a false alarm that looks exactly like a real finding. Add the project form of the command or a linking prerequisite, name the credential required, and state explicitly that empty output means THE COMMAND FAILED and not that the flag is unset. Also remove or earn the claim that the command prints the configured value and its age, which the reviewer could not observe. F5: the modal body discriminator overstates. A card build renders a card position modal with NO card field whenever phase one fails, on a 503, a network error or an expired session, which matches the balance row and would make an operator conclude Balance on a card build. Promote the CTA sub line to the PRIMARY discriminator, since it is a pure function of the inlined flag in every state, and mark the Stripe field row as conditional on phase one having succeeded. F4: attach the pointer to the flat claim near the top of the section that states which settlement travellers get, not only to the table, or soften that claim to name the environment as its source. F6: name the login required for the log query, matching how the card provider corroboration already discloses its access requirement. F7: add reload discipline, a fresh private window and a hard reload with cache disabled, because an operator with the site already open reads the previous deploy bundle and gets a confident wrong answer. F8: move the disclosure that the card arm writes a production booking row and mints a live mode payment intent UP into the sentence that currently claims the steps move no money, so a reader learns it before committing to the walk rather than after. F9 and F10: replace the fragile fourth paragraph citation with a line citation or a quoted sentence, and make the cross reference a real link like every other one in the section. F3 YOU CANNOT FIX AND MUST NOT FAKE. The reviewer found the primary procedure has never actually been executed, because running it needs a browser and a signed in QA account. Do NOT invent an execution record and do NOT write a date you did not observe. Instead mark that step explicitly as PENDING FIRST EXECUTION, say plainly that it is derived from source and not yet observed against production, and note that manual browser verification is owned by QA rather than by whoever writes this doc. Recording the gap honestly is the deliverable. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash character anywhere in any line you add, including the commit message and PR comment. Push to the SAME branch docs/settlement-empirical-check so PR 2765 updates in place. Do not open a new PR. Do not merge. Add one comment to PR 2765 listing what changed per finding, and naming F3 as deliberately not closed. Omit any Co-Authored-By trailer. | docs/settlement-empirical-check

